.                 keep if kidgeb01 != -2  //these persons never have children. 
(10,594 observations deleted)

.                 drop if kidgeb01 < 0 //Also drop [-1] No Answer [-2] Does not
>  apply [-3] Answer improbable
(99 observations deleted)

.                 
. 
.                 *Drop years before child1 was born
.                 drop if syear < kidgeb01 
(960 observations deleted)

. 
. 
.                 *(1b) Keep only if sex of child is known 
.                 drop if kidsex01 < 0 // missings 
(38 observations deleted)

. 
.         
.                 *(2) have one child only (dropped once second child arrives).
>  Except if twins, then counted as 'having daughter' if both of them are girls
>  
. 
.                 gen twins = 1 if kidgeb01==kidgeb02 & kidmon01==kidmon02 & ki
> dgeb02 != -2 //month and year of birth same, and second child present. 
(23,279 missing values generated)

.                 drop if twins==1 & kidsex02 < 0 // if 2nd twins gender unknow
> n 
(0 observations deleted)

.                 
.                 drop if syear > kidgeb02 & twins !=1  //drop observations (su
> rveyyears) once 2nd child is born (except first child is twin)
(22,394 observations deleted)

.                 drop if syear > kidgeb03 & twins ==1 //drop observations (sur
> veyyears) once 3rd child is born (if first child is twin)
(252 observations deleted)

. 
. 
. * GENERATE VARIABLES * 
. 
.         *(1)generate dummy variable for participants sex
.         fre sex

sex -- Gender
------------------------------------------------------------------
                     |      Freq.    Percent      Valid       Cum.
---------------------+--------------------------------------------
Valid   1 [1] Male   |        402      45.12      45.12      45.12
        2 [2] Female |        489      54.88      54.88     100.00
        Total        |        891     100.00     100.00           
------------------------------------------------------------------

.         gen d_sex = sex-1

.         fre d_sex

d_sex
-----------------------------------------------------------
              |      Freq.    Percent      Valid       Cum.
--------------+--------------------------------------------
Valid   0     |        402      45.12      45.12      45.12
        1     |        489      54.88      54.88     100.00
        Total |        891     100.00     100.00           
-----------------------------------------------------------

.         label variable d_sex "Sex of participants (0=Male, 1=Female)"

. 
.         *(2)Generate dummy variable for whether participant`s child is a girl
>  (1) or boy (0)
.         gen d_daughter = 1 if kidsex01== 2 //girl
(492 missing values generated)

.         replace d_daughter=0 if kidsex01==1 //boy       
(492 real changes made)

.         drop if twins==1 & d_daughter==0 & kidsex02==2 //drop if first child 
> is boy, but second twin is girl 
(0 observations deleted)

.         drop if twins==1 & d_daughter==1 & kidsex02==1 //drop if first child 
> is girl, but second twin is boy 
(6 observations deleted)

.         label variable d_daughter "Sex of first child (0=son, 1=daughter)"

.         fre d_daughter

d_daughter -- Sex of first child (0=son, 1=daughter)
-----------------------------------------------------------
              |      Freq.    Percent      Valid       Cum.
--------------+--------------------------------------------
Valid   0     |        492      55.59      55.59      55.59
        1     |        393      44.41      44.41     100.00
        Total |        885     100.00     100.00           
-----------------------------------------------------------

.         
.         *(3)Construct total hours respondent does childcare, errands, housewo
> rk: 'CareAndHouse'                 
.         gen CaH1 = pli0044_v3 if pli0044_v3 >= 0 //Childcare during week
(96 missing values generated)

.         gen CaH2 = pli0040 if pli0040 >= 0       //errands during week
(139 missing values generated)

.         gen CaH3 = pli0043_h if pli0043_h >= 0   //housework during week
(135 missing values generated)

. 
.                 *Keep only persons with all items answered:
.                 egen rownonmiss =  rownonmiss(CaH1 CaH2 CaH3)

.                 keep if rownonmiss==3
(179 observations deleted)

.                 
.                 *Construct variable indicating 
.                 egen CareAndHouse =  rowtotal(CaH1 CaH2 CaH3)  

.                 
. 
.         *(4)Construct variable for 'relative' hours (comparing partners hours
>  to each other) 
. 
.                 *First identify partners (pgpartnr). Partners need to be in t
> he same household.
.                 keep if !missing(pgpartz) & pgpartz != 0 & pgpartz != 9 //if 
> pgpartz is 0, or [9] no partner (identified) 
(64 observations deleted)

.                 *If PGPARTZ is coded 1, 2, 3 or 4, a partnership was defined 
> and PGPARTNR is then assigned the value of the unchanging person ID number (=
> PERSNR) of the partner.
.                 drop if pgpartz==5 //drop also if PGPARTZ==5 (pgpartnr is the
> n -2)
(0 observations deleted)

. 
.                 *Generate 'partnermerge' that assigns couples the same id, wh
> ich corresponds either to theirs or their partners pid.
.                 gen partnermerge =      .
(642 missing values generated)

.                 replace partnermerge = pid  if pid < pgpartnr
(355 real changes made)

.                 replace partnermerge = pgpartnr if pgpartnr < pid
(287 real changes made)

. 
.                 *partners should also be in the same household:
.                 gen notsamehouse= 1 if partnermerge==partnermerge[_n+1] & hid
>  != hid[_n+1]
(639 missing values generated)

.                 drop if notsamehouse== 1 & (syear==syear[_n+1] | syear==syear
> [_n-1])
(0 observations deleted)

. 
. 
.                 *create variable 'partners_CareAndHouse' indicating partners 
> hours
.                 bysort partnermerge syear: gen partners_CareAndHouse = CareAn
> dHouse[_n+1] if syear==syear[_n+1]
(384 missing values generated)

.                 bysort partnermerge syear: replace partners_CareAndHouse = Ca
> reAndHouse[_n-1] if syear==syear[_n-1] & missing(partners_CareAndHouse)
(258 real changes made)

. 
. 
.                 *How much hours each partner spends relative to the other (ma
> inly to identify if both partners have a value)
.                 *Then take Latest survey year which has info on relative_h 
.                 gen relative_h = (CareAndHouse*100)/(CareAndHouse + partners_
> CareAndHouse) 
(126 missing values generated)

.                 sort partnermerge syear

.                 
.                 keep if !missing(relative_h)
(126 observations deleted)

.                 bysort partnermerge syear: gen n_partner = _N

.                 keep if n_partner == 2 //keep only years in which both couple
> s present
(0 observations deleted)

. 
.                 bysort partnermerge (syear): gen latest = syear == syear[_N] 
>  //identify latest year==1 

.                 keep if latest==1
(330 observations deleted)

. 
. 
.         *(5)Create the IV: `equality' (equality in the household)
.         *We want 1 to be fully equal, so:  1-   (|(my hours/total)-0.5 | *2)
.         * 1- (|(CareAndHouse/(CareAndHouse + partners_CareAndHouse))-0.5 | *2
> )
.         gen share =     (CareAndHouse/(CareAndHouse + partners_CareAndHouse))
> -0.5

.         replace share = share*(-1) if share <0
(90 real changes made)

.         gen equality = 1- (share*2)

.         sum equality, d //0-1

                          equality
-------------------------------------------------------------
      Percentiles      Smallest
 1%            0              0
 5%     .0740741              0
