99%            1              1       Kurtosis       2.549883

. 
. 
. 
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H3 * 
. 
.         * We assume that the division of childcare and housework tasks among 
> couples (equality) is a good measure of gender equality in the household (hyp
> othesis 3), 
.         * if having a daughter, the respondent is more likely to have higher 
> gender equality in the household (a higher score on scale indicating equality
>  within the household regarding division of childcare and household tasks).
.         * Accordingly, we run a linear OLS regression analysis with `equality
> ' as dependent variable and the dummy variable `d_daughter' as independent va
> riable
. 
.         reg equality d_daughter, cluster(hid) 

Linear regression                               Number of obs     =        186
                                                F(1, 92)          =       0.24
                                                Prob > F          =     0.6264
                                                R-squared         =     0.0025
                                                Root MSE          =     .25155

                                   (Std. err. adjusted for 93 clusters in hid)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
             |               Robust
    equality | Coefficient  std. err.      t    P>|t|     [95% conf. interval]
-------------+----------------------------------------------------------------
  d_daughter |   .0252403   .0516689     0.49   0.626    -.0773786    .1278593
       _cons |   .4051646   .0336525    12.04   0.000     .3383277    .4720014
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

. 
. 
. * EXTRACT AND EXPORT RESULTS * 
. 
.         * Extract the required statistics
. 
.                 * (i) coefficient estimate
.                 local coefficient = _b[d_daughter]

. 
.                 * (ii) standard error
.                 local se = _se[d_daughter]

. 
.                 * (iii) family of the test statistic (e.g. z, t, F, Chi²)
.                 local test_stat_family = "t"

. 
.                 * (iv) residual and model degrees of freedom (DFs) if applica
> ble
.                 local df_residual = e(df_r)

.                 local df_model = e(df_m)

. 
.                 * (v) p-value
.                 local p_value = _b[d_daughter] / _se[d_daughter]

.                 local p_value = 2 * ttail(e(df_r), abs(`p_value'))

. 
.                 * (vi) number of observations
.                 local num_obs = e(N)

. 
.                 * (vii) number of participants
.                 quietly levelsof pid if e(sample), local(participants)

.                 local num_participants : word count `participants'

. 
.                 * (viii) interpretation based of directionality and p-value
.                 local interpretation "positive coefficient is in line with hy
> pothesis"

.                         
.         // Display the saved statistics
.         di "Coefficient: `coefficient'"
Coefficient: .025240305710061

.         di "Standard Error: `se'"
Standard Error: .0516689261501236

.         di "Test Statistic Family: `test_stat_family'"
